 2 AZs ensure web tier survives single-AZ failure; ASG self-healing replaces failed instances automatically; CloudFront edge caching provides resilience against origin outages.\n\n*Performance Efficiency:* t3.small instances deliver 2× throughput of t3.micro at 2× hourly cost, meeting peak demand with headroom; ASG scales to only 2 instances during average-load periods (150 req/s origin demand requires 2 instances at 80 req/s each), reducing waste relative to running maximum capacity; CloudFront caches 50% of requests, cutting origin load from 1,500 to 750 req/s at peak.\n\n*Cost Optimization:* ASG minimum of 2 instances during off-peak periods and flexible scaling during peak (60 hours) distributes compute cost; t3.small provides sufficient capacity at manageable cost; monthly total of $713.20 is 4.9% below budget, leaving headroom for growth; reserved instance or savings plan purchases could further reduce costs.",
